    "k_nearest": "HERB_V4_K, 5 unless named: the number of clusters each side's nearness is cut into over the border (`v4_walk.levels`).",
    "offline": "HERB_V4_OFFLINE=on reads the first call's answer from the cache and raises where it is missing; off asks the model on a miss.",
    "retrieval": "The border is every branch of the tree whose name stands in the question word for word (`scope_by_name`), the chunks outside it out of the pool. Inside it (`v4_walk.cloud_combo`): each chunk's closest eligible tag to a query tag, with the query's facets as an influence on the tag relationship (`v4_walk.facet_influenced_nearness`: the facet net reads the query tags against the question and the description, the middle reading per facet; its level among that facet's levels over the graph's edges is the facet's weight; an edge's weight is the tag's closeness plus, per facet, that weight times where the edge stands in the facet's ranking), and the chunk descriptions' closeness to the question with the border's names taken out, each cut into HERB_V4_K clusters; a chunk's step is its two levels added; the parents holding the majority of the chunks on the first two steps are the scope, whose chunks come first inside a step, then the two standings added. What is handed over, in that order (`_hand_over`): no message of a channel apart; of a batch of pull requests only the product's own; of a batch of Slack messages only the conversations that are not about another project's pull request, each conversation whole where it first shows; any other chunk as it is. From the graph (`product_persons`, through the person-to-chunk edges): a channel is apart when it has employees and none of them is tied to another channel or to a meeting of the product; the product's people are the employees of its other channels and of its meetings. From the records, through the chunk's pointer: a pull request is the product's own when its author is one of the product's people; a conversation is a channel's messages between its long gaps (`v4_walk.conversations`, no length given); it is about another project's when a message of it links to a pull request that is not the product's own and none links to an own pull request or to a document of the product. The handing over is the agent's find, read off the benchmark's own account of the distraction it holds (arXiv 2506.23139), not his concept; it never reads the question.",
